Generate a TLS certificate

A TLS certificate is required during silo setup and will be used for TLS termination on the silo-specific UI/API DNS name. The certificate’s DNS SAN can either be the silo’s fully-qualified domain name (FQDN):

```
$SILO_NAME.sys.$OXIDE_DOMAIN_NAME
```

or a wildcard domain name:

```
*.sys.$OXIDE_DOMAIN_NAME
```

For production deployments, use a certificate from a trusted Certificate Authority (CA). For testing or development, a self-signed certificate may be sufficient.

